  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN290.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">iravukkuṟikkaṭ ṭalaimakaṉ ciṟaippuṟattāṉākat tōḻikkuc colluvāḷāyt talaimakaḷ colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What SHE said as one who speaks to the confidante when HE was behind the hedge during the night tryst.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN290.1">
        <l>kuṭumik kokkiṉ paiṅkāṟ pēṭai</l>
        <l>yiruñcēṟ ṟaḷḷa ṉāṭpulam pōkiya</l>
        <l>koḻumīṉ valcip puṉṟalaic ciṟā<supplied>a</supplied>r</l>
        <l>nuṇñā ṇav<supplied>va</supplied>laic cēval paṭṭeṉa</l>
        <l>valkuṟu po<supplied>ḻu</supplied>tiṉ melkirai <supplied>mi</supplied>caiyātu</l>
        <l>paitaṟ piḷḷai taḻīi yoyyeṉa</l>
        <l>vaṅkaṭ peṇṇai yaṉpuṟa naraluñ</l>
        <l>ciṟupaḵ ṟolkuṭip perunīrc cērppaṉ</l>
        <l>kaḻicēr puṉṉai yaḻi<supplied>pū</supplied>ṅ kāṉaṟ</l>
        <l>ṟaṇavā neñcamoṭu tamiyaṉ vantunam</l>
        <l>maṇavā muṉṉu <supplied>mevaṉō</supplied> tōḻi</l>
        <l>veṇṭukō<supplied>ṭ</supplied> ṭiyāṉai viṟaṟpōrk kuṭṭuvaṉ</l>
        <l>ṟeṇṭiraip parappiṟ ṟoṇṭi muṉṟuṟaic</l>
        <l>curumpuṇa malarnta perunta ṇeytaṉ</l>
        <l>maṇiyēr māṇala morīip</l>
        <l>poṉṉēr <supplied>va</supplied>ṇṇaṅ koṇṭaveṉ kaṇṇē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="8">The man from the coast of the great water with many small old hamlets,</l>
        <l corresp="1">where the green-legged female of the crested egret</l>
        <l corresp="7">calls out lovingly in the palmyra tree there,</l>
        <l corresp="6">dolefully(?), embracing [her] young ones, suffering,</l>
        <l corresp="5">without having tasted soft prey [still] at the time when night falls,</l>
        <l corresp="4">because [her] cock has been caught in the pretty net with fine strings</l>
        <l corresp="3">of the ruddy-headed youngsters with fat fish for [their] food</l>
        <l corresp="2">who had gone to the fields [early in] the day, with dark muddy mire,</l>
        <l>– even before he came alone, with a heart that does not leave off,</l>
        <l>to the seashore grove with flowers perishing on the Puṉṉai trees close to the backwaters,</l>
        <l corresp="9-11">[and] united with us – what [is this], friend? –</l>
        <l corresp="16">my eyes have taken a colour like gold,</l>
        <l corresp="15">abandoning [their] glorious beauty, resembling the sapphires</l>
        <l corresp="14">of big cool blue waterlilies come to bloom for bees to eat</l>
        <l corresp="13">in the front ghat of Toṇṭi, with [its] expanse of clear waves,</l>
        <l corresp="12">[belonging to] Kuṭṭuvaṉ of victorious battle, with white-tusked elephants.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="alternate" sameAs="11">
        <l corresp="11b-d 16d">Why does he keep approaching my eyes, friend,</l>
        <l corresp="16a-c">that have taken a colour like gold, ...</l>
        <l corresp="11a">– without uniting with us ...</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
